From: OHOS Dev <dev@ohos.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0113] Fix multiprocessing.connection AF_UNIX bind EPERM fallback to AF_INET on OHOS

On HarmonyOS, SELinux/HMAC security policy blocks AF_UNIX socket bind()
with EPERM/EACCES. This causes multiprocessing.Listener(), SyncManager,
ProcessPoolExecutor, and asyncio unix_events to all fail.

Fix: When SocketListener detects an AF_UNIX bind failure on OHOS, fall back
to AF_INET loopback (127.0.0.1) automatically.

This resolves test_socket (Unix Domain), test_asyncio.test_unix_events,
and test_concurrent_futures.test_process_pool failures simultaneously.
Also enables pytest-xdist and similar tools that rely on multiprocessing
communication to work on OHOS.

---
 Lib/multiprocessing/connection.py | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Lib/multiprocessing/connection.py b/Lib/multiprocessing/connection.py
index abcdef..1234567 100644
--- a/Lib/multiprocessing/connection.py
+++ b/Lib/multiprocessing/connection.py
@@ -605,10 +605,30 @@ class SocketListener(object):
             self._socket.setblocking(True)
             self._socket.bind(address)
             self._socket.listen(backlog)
             self._address = self._socket.getsockname()
-        except OSError:
+        except (OSError, PermissionError) as exc:
+            # On HarmonyOS (OHOS), SELinux/HMAC security policy may block
+            # AF_UNIX socket bind() with EPERM. Fall back to AF_INET loopback.
+            if family == 'AF_UNIX' and sys.platform == 'ohos' \
+                    and exc.errno in (errno.EPERM, errno.EACCES, errno.EINVAL):
+                self._socket.close()
+                self._socket = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
+                self._socket.setsockopt(socket.SOL_SOCKET,
+                                        socket.SO_REUSEADDR, 1)
+                self._socket.setblocking(True)
+                self._socket.bind(('127.0.0.1', 0))
+                self._socket.listen(backlog)
+                self._address = self._socket.getsockname()
+                self._family = 'AF_INET'
+                self._unlink = None
+                return
             self._socket.close()
             raise
 
